  "qualifications": [
    "Four URL parse cases and two setters follow the WHATWG URL standard on WebKit and differ on Chromium 156 (space in a host, \"|\" in a path, file:c: drive case, file://localhost, the mailto protocol setter, search = \"?\").",
    "URLPattern groups come in engine (pattern) order on WebKit, and in JavaScript object order (integer-like keys first) on Chromium, for /:name/(\\d+).",
    "Fable erases Some null to None, so a null base parses without a base in the browser and raises ArgumentNullException natively.",
    "URLSearchParams.getAll and the sequence<sequence<USVString>> init arm are NUL-terminated natively; the provider sends pairs through the record arm."
  ]
